| **Desktop PC** | Expand the Pygame demo: add sound effects, timer, high‑score leaderboard saved to disk. |
| **Mobile App** | Port to Kivy (Python) or use React Native / Flutter for cross‑platform UI. |
| **Online Multiplayer** | Host a simple Node.js backend storing puzzle state; players compete to finish fastest. |
| **Educational Tool** | Hook up a database of images tied to learning topics; track progress over many puzzles. |
| **Artistic Interactivity** | Implement custom edge shapes (triangular, curved) using SVG paths or CSS clip-path. |

Let me know which direction excites you most—or if you'd like deeper dives into any particular part!
